From: Timothy Tan <2604749@sit.singaporetech.edu.sg>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:40:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Web app: same account rules as the terminal, no fixed
 secret key, debugger off by default

- Registration (page and API) now uses InputValidator, the terminal's rules:
  3-20 letters, digits or _ for usernames, 8-64 characters with a letter and a
  digit for passwords. Usernames are not case-sensitive, as in the terminal.
  A non-text username or password from the API is a 400, not a crash.
- Without FLASK_SECRET_KEY a random key is made at each start instead of the
  fixed 'dev-only-change-me', which anyone reading the code could use to
  forge a login cookie.
- python app.py only turns on the Flask debugger with FLASK_DEBUG=1.
- gunicorn is added to requirements.txt, so the Docker web command in the
  README works.
- Tests in tests/test_web_security.py; README and .env.example updated.
